Audit EVERY Firestore read/write path in the entire application.

Select one canonical, consistent ownership-aware database structure. Prefer clearly scoped user subcollections if appropriate, but decide based on real existing data and usage patterns.

Then:

- Update rules and queries consistently.
- Implement an idempotent migration for legacy stored records where necessary.
- Prevent cross-user reads, writes, list queries, and ownership changes.
- Enforce schemas, size limits, allowed fields, immutable identifiers, and timestamps.
- Verify actual Firestore query compatibility.
- Do not silently delete, relocate, or overwrite student content.
- Test with Firebase Emulator using two or more distinct user identities.
- Verify permission-denied errors are handled gracefully in the UI.

Test account switching, sign-out, deletion, fresh login, refresh, and cross-device synchronization.

